	'kaf8cfe54' => 'Core Values in Daily Craft',
	'kb0629e5a' => 'Graduate stories',
	'kb074e150' => 'Students arrive, sanitise styling stations, inspect tool rolls and prepare mannequin blocks for the morning session.',
	'kb0b6b53c' => 'What are the daily hours and weekly schedule?',
	'kb0bdc3f4' => 'Amara Lindqvist',
	'kb0dc7ac0' => 'Every instructor at Kesho College is an active, experienced craft practitioner who balances teaching with commercial client floor work. Our teaching team guides students through direct demonstration, close supervision, and honest professional feedback every day.',
	'kb15a920a' => 'See tuition &amp; intakes →',
	'kb73130d6' => 'The high volume of afternoon clients in the Student Salon helped him develop speed and clean sectioning habits without sacrificing precision. After finishing his certificate, Jonah chose to rent a chair at an established independent barbershop. Working as an independent chair renter, he manages his own clients, schedules appointments, and applies the hygiene and tool maintenance standards ingrained during his daily training at Harbour Lane.',
	'kb7716cb3' => 'First Saturday of each month, 10:00<br>14 Harbour Lane, Lindmoor',
	'kb7b44874' => 'Client communication is treated as a core trade skill, training juniors to conduct thorough consultations, ask clear questions, and manage expectations calmly. Finally, our students take full responsibility for tool hygiene, station sanitation, and evening clean-down. These shared standards build working habits that salon owners respect and junior stylists rely on throughout their working careers.',
	'kb805bb90' => 'An informal conversation with Clara Weiss about your goals and schedule.',
	'kba2a9c6c' => 'Length',
	'kbaab1431' => 'Who the intake is for',
	'kbac568b5' => 'Apply →',
	'kbbd71fa4' => 'Every morning begins with an instructor demonstrating core cutting, styling or colour techniques to a semicircle of students before mannequin practice starts on the salon floor.',
	'kbd5cfc29' => 'To complete your application following your interview, you will need to submit a completed application form, valid government-issued photographic identification confirming you are aged 16 or older, and contact details for one character reference. Once Clara Weiss issues your written acceptance letter, you have fourteen days to pay the €300 deposit and confirm your place.',
	'kbfa4451c' => 'How are tuition fees structured and paid?',
	'kc0095550' => 'What does the four-step admissions process involve?',
	'kc1fd9c29' => 'To maintain deliberate, high-standard teaching across every programme, Kesho College caps all cohorts at a maximum of 14 students. In the practical training areas and during client service sessions, we maintain a strict floor ratio of one instructor to seven students.',
	'kc2d2a39a' => 'Evening Colour Course',
	'kc32a2c81' => 'In addition to tuition, students enrolling in the Hairdressing Diploma and Barbering Certificate purchase the mandatory college kit for €420. This comprehensive kit contains all scissors, clippers, training mannequins, and specialist tools required for daily class and practical salon floor training.',
	'kc63e2429' => 'Nails',
	'kc63f65b4' => 'Weekly Schedule and Assessment',
	'kc6602eb7' => 'Vocational hairdressing and beauty education for future salon juniors. Founded 2009.',
	'kc678ab58' => 'Our admissions process is designed to be accessible, transparent, and focused entirely on practical suitability. Applicants must be at least 16 years of age by the start date of their chosen intake.',
	'kc6d90683' => 'Students are responsible for bringing their college-issued tool kit to every session, including shears, clippers, sectioning clips, combs, and brushes. Cleanliness is paramount: blades must be oiled daily, guards sanitised between uses, and combs submerged in sterilising solution. Developing this daily personal care and equipment readiness ensures seamless integration into professional salon environments after graduation.',
	'kc7db2bf9' => 'Can members of the public book appointments at the Student Salon?',
	'kc85f6d0b' => 'Six ways to start',
	'kc85fc1b7' => 'The 3-month Nail Technology Certificate costs €2,400, starting on 19 April 2027, with detailed training in natural nail care, extensions, cuticle work, and sanitation protocols. Both certificate pathways require a €300 deposit to secure a chair, with small cohorts capped at 14 learners ensuring constant practical feedback from lead tutors.',
	'kc8bc6f26' => 'Founded in 2009 by colour specialist Amara Lindqvist, Kesho College prepares future salon juniors through structured, hand-to-hand craft education. We believe professional hairdressing and beauty skills develop best when students practise alongside working stylists every day.',
	'kcaa986a6' => 'Class Sizes and Floor Supervision',
	'kcb20d178' => 'Interview',
	'kcbb37401' => 'Stories',
	'kcbd8944d' => 'Open morning',
	'kcc8d0518' => 'Teachers',
	'kcca6c16c' => 'For those focused specifically on classic and modern men\'s grooming, the 6-month Barbering Certificate costs €4,600 and begins on 11 January 2027. Both courses require an equipment kit fee of €420 and a €300 deposit upon acceptance, with remaining tuition payable across three instalments.',
	'kcdc09d76' => 'Curriculum and Core Modules',
	'kce8ae9da' => 'Email',
	'kced83394' => 'Yes, our Student Salon is open to the public Tuesday to Saturday from 10:00 to 16:00 at 14 Harbour Lane in Lindmoor. Local clients can book haircuts with blow-dry finishes for €18, chemical colour services starting from €35, and classic beard trims for €10. All appointments are carried out by supervised students with tutor guidance at every stage. Because our trainees work thoroughly and check each step with instructors, clients should expect treatments to take somewhat longer than standard high-street salon appointments.',
	'kcf0df42a' => 'Enrolment at Kesho College follows a clear four-step path to ensure mutual fit between student and school. Step one begins with visiting an open morning, held on the first Saturday of each month at 10:00.',
	'kcfca85ba' => 'The diploma curriculum is structured around five core training modules delivered over 12 months. Students begin with fundamental scissor work and geometry, mastering blunt bobs, graduation, and long layers before advancing into modern texturising. The colour and chemistry module covers formulation, scalp protection, foil placement, and corrective treatments.',
	'kd0a91c83' => 'Where they are now',
	'kd0fbda98' => 'Page not found',
	'kd260287a' => 'English · Chinese · Japanese · French · German',
	'kd2f6e855' => 'Operational discipline and student well-being are guided by our dedicated administrative team. Samuel Reyes manages the Student Salon, overseeing daily public appointment bookings, stock management, client reception, and trainee floor schedules while enforcing our 1:7 supervision ratio.',
	'kd4251b01' => 'Our Foundation and Teaching Method',
	'kd62dc1bb' => 'Hana Kowalski',
	'kd6fb2315' => 'Service Menu and Pricing',
	'kd9e9d534' => 'Tuition &amp; intakes →',
	'kdab5873e' => 'Students repeat what they have seen on mannequin blocks, with one-on-one correction from the instructor at the elbow.',
	'kdba5c922' => 'Dress Code and Equipment Requirements',
	'kdc25c1cb' => 'Our training salon and administrative offices are situated at 14 Harbour Lane in Lindmoor, just a short walk from local bus and transit routes. The administrative office is open Monday to Friday from 09:00 to 17:30 to handle student admissions, fee payments, and general enquiries.',
	'kdd45af1d' => '“The repetition on mannequin blocks gave me real muscle memory before I touched a client’s hair. When I stepped onto a commercial floor as a junior, the pace and the consultations felt familiar.”',
	'kddb6f55c' => 'Book a place',
	'kdf589719' => 'Notes from the training floor',
	'kdfe6076e' => 'Colour',
	'ke0346ab1' => 'Tuition and intake dates',
	'ke057e80d' => 'Practical trial',
	'ke1671797' => 'e',
	'ke24ccf09' => 'Hands first, theory alongside',
	'ke3899bd8' => 'Training at Kesho College runs Monday to Friday from 08:45 to 17:00, mirroring the daily rhythms and operational pressures of a working commercial salon.',
	'ke3b481d5' => '1 day',
	'ke3bd27fd' => 'Offer &amp; deposit',
	'ke45dcbba' => '19 Apr 2027',
	'ke547acd1' => 'It concentrates on modern foil placement, grey coverage, balayage transitions, and colour correction principles. For prospective students wanting hands-on experience before submitting an application, our 1-day Taster Saturday costs €95 and runs on the first Saturday of each month. It provides a full day of basic sectioning, blow-drying, and campus life.',
	'ke7bcef43' => 'When the next class begins',
	'ke7e3865a' => 'Our core curriculum offers full-time foundations: the 12-month Hairdressing Diploma, the 6-month Barbering Certificate and the 4-month Makeup Artistry Certificate. For specialised study or a first taste, there are the 3-month Nail Technology Certificate, the 10-week Evening Colour Course and a monthly one-day Taster Saturday.',
	'ke81f3370' => 'Amara Lindqvist is the founder and principal of Kesho College, directing our colour curriculum and overall academic standards since opening the school in 2009. A specialist in formulation chemistry, corrective work, and complex foil placement, she continues to train students in the patience and scientific accuracy necessary for modern colour work.',
	'ke8be0a43' => 'Four steps',
	'ke9522b55' => '6 months, full-time',
	'ke96e04ca' => 'Kesho College provides transparent, straightforward tuition fees and fixed intake schedules across all six of our vocational courses. We support students with a three-instalment payment structure and clear fee schedules established before classes begin.',
	'ke9baaa74' => 'The day',
	'keac9f099' => 'For students pursuing focused beauty careers, Kesho College delivers two modular part-time certificate courses at our Lindmoor campus. The 4-month Makeup Artistry Certificate costs €3,200 and begins on 8 February 2027, covering facial anatomy, skin prep, bridal styles, photographic balance, and theatre character work.',
	'keaed15e4' => 'Block practice on mannequins',
	'ked400fdc' => 'Aisha Rahman joined Kesho College in 2023 for our 4-month Makeup Artistry Certificate, studying skin preparation, facial anatomy, and camera lighting under Inês Duarte. The small cohort of 14 students allowed for immediate daily critique, helping Aisha master delicate bridal skin finishes and bolder theatrical character design.',
	'kedf7553d' => 'Find us',
	'keeaec18e' => 'Teaching hours run Monday to Friday from 08:45 to 17:00. The public Student Salon operates Tuesday to Saturday from 10:00 to 16:00. Visitors are welcome to call into our street-level reception to pick up course prospectuses or schedule an informal campus tour with our admissions staff.',
	'keedc40c0' => 'The Student Salon welcomes public clients Tuesday to Saturday from 10:00 to 16:00, while remaining closed on Sundays and Mondays. Advanced bookings are highly recommended due to high local demand and limited chair availability each afternoon.',
	'kef0bb29c' => 'Aisha Rahman',
	'kefbc513f' => 'Our daily training is anchored by three practical values: deliberate handwork, honest client communication, and disciplined salon maintenance. We believe technical precision must always come before speed, requiring students to measure section widths carefully and control blade angles with complete intention.',
	'kf0108495' => 'Taught by working stylists',
	'kf1e8a2ee' => 'Lunch',
	'kf416a5b7' => '12 months, full-time',
	'kf5641b86' => 'Nail Technology →',
	'kf653b8ae' => 'Okafor',
	'kf80e9cde' => 'No previous hairdressing, barbering, or beauty experience is needed to apply for any of our diploma or certificate programmes. We teach every discipline from the absolute beginning, starting with basic scissor control, sectioning angles, comb posture, and tool hygiene. Our structured training method demonstrates every skill clearly before you practice on mannequin blocks, allowing complete beginners to build confidence gradually. What matters most during our admissions process is your willingness to listen, your dedication to deliberate daily practice, and your enthusiasm for learning a manual craft alongside working professionals.',
	'kf8546451' => '12 months · from €8,400',
	'kf9de1ed4' => 'At 13:30, the Student Salon opens to the public, welcoming local clients for booked cuts, colours, and grooming treatments. Trainees run thorough consultations, formulate shades, and perform cuts under our strict 1:7 instructor supervision ratio, with mentors checking every perimeter line and colour balance before the client departs.',
	'kfbfd610a' => 'Graduates of Kesho College carry deliberate handwork, commercial salon awareness, and technical confidence into the professional hairdressing and beauty sector. Here, three past students share their educational journey from mannequin benches to independent salon chairs.',
	'kfc062c1f' => 'Kesho Colleg',
	'kfcef2ec0' => 'The Kesho College Student Salon is our live commercial floor where advanced trainees deliver hairdressing, barbering, and beauty services to the public. All treatments are performed under the close supervision of working instructors to maintain strict salon standards.',
	'kfd55acdf' => 'Book a practical trial',
	'kfdecb33a' => 'To assist learners with budgeting, tuition for our longer diploma and certificate courses can be paid in three equal instalments spread across the study duration. Upon receiving a formal written offer of admission, an applicant must secure their place by paying a non-refundable deposit of €300, which is deducted from their first tuition instalment.',
	'kfff3e55e' => 'Admissions',
	'search_results' => 'Search results for: %s',
);
